# Copy this to `.env` to change the defaults. install.sh creates an empty
# private file when none exists. Direct Compose reads it in this directory.
#
# Running a SECOND Sill on this host: every commented-out name below has to
# change, not just SILL_DB_CONTAINER. docker-compose.yml names four
# containers and binds three host ports, and the Compose project name (which
# prefixes the volume names) defaults to the directory it runs from —
# `backend`, identically for every clone. See the README's "Run a second Sill
# side by side". install.sh, verify.sh, and upgrade.sh all read this file.

# --- Compose project (volume-name prefix) ---
# COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=sill

# --- Restart policy ---
# All four services default to `unless-stopped`: they come back after a
# reboot, a Docker/OrbStack engine restart, or a crash, but stay down if you
# deliberately ran `docker compose stop`.
#
# The container engine must be running for its restart policy to take effect.
# Set to `no` to start the stack by hand.
# SILL_RESTART_POLICY=unless-stopped

# --- Network exposure ---
# The three host ports now bind to 127.0.0.1 by default; the previous
# implicit default was 0.0.0.0 (all interfaces). SILL_BIND_ADDR can opt in
# to a different address. Postgres uses trust authentication: anyone who
# can reach it gets access without a password. RabbitMQ's management UI also
# ships with known default credentials. Keep all ports private.
# For a specific interface address, also set POSTGRES_HOST to that address
# so the local MCP launcher and seed import use the same interface.
# SILL_BIND_ADDR=127.0.0.1
# POSTGRES_HOST=localhost

# --- Postgres ---
# Container name lets multiple Sill instances coexist (e.g. test vs prod).
SILL_DB_CONTAINER=sill_db
POSTGRES_DB=sill
POSTGRES_USER=sill
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=sill_password
# Bump if 5432 collides with another Postgres on this host.
POSTGRES_PORT=5432

# --- Embeddings ---
# LOCKED at install. Changing the model later requires a schema rebuild
# because vector column types are wired to EMBEDDING_DIMENSION via
# the app.embedding_dimension Postgres GUC.
# First boot downloads the model weights; subsequent starts reuse the cache.
EMBEDDING_MODEL_ID=unsloth/embeddinggemma-300m
EMBEDDING_DIMENSION=768
# SILL_EMBEDDINGS_CONTAINER=sill_embeddings

# Managed install/reset use the Docker engine architecture (arm64 or amd64).
# Shell exports take precedence over .env; explicit EMBEDDING_IMAGE and
# EMBEDDING_PLATFORM override the managed defaults. If only the platform
# changes, managed scripts select its matching default image.
#
# Direct Compose defaults to a pinned linux/amd64 CPU image. On an arm64
# engine, put these two exact settings in .env for native direct Compose:
# EMBEDDING_IMAGE=ghcr.io/huggingface/text-embeddings-inference@sha256:798cd7615e060a72ccbdf19aa0ada52289c6a0147490195bafaece6ce04d70f1
# EMBEDDING_PLATFORM=linux/arm64
#
# Managed scripts pin the revision below for the default model only. For
# direct Compose, also set it explicitly when using the default model.
# A custom model uses its own revision (default main) unless you set one.
# EMBEDDING_REVISION=bfa3c846ac738e62aa61806ef9112d34acb1dc5a
# EMBEDDING_MAX_BATCH_TOKENS=2048
# SILL_INSTALL_WAIT_HEALTHY_S=1800
#
# Both pinned images were checked with the same unprompted model at 768
# dimensions. Changing the model or dimension is a separate data migration.
# Mac containers run TEI on CPU. Native ARM was exercised on an M-series
# Mac; the amd64 image was exercised under emulation there.

# --- RabbitMQ ---
RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_USER=sill
RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_PASS=sill_password
RABBITMQ_PORT=5672
# Host ports must be <= 65535.
RABBITMQ_MANAGEMENT_PORT=15672
# SILL_RABBITMQ_CONTAINER=sill_rabbitmq

# --- Maintenance worker ---
# SILL_MAINTENANCE_WORKER_CONTAINER=sill_maintenance_worker

# --- Hook environment (read by plugin/hooks/*) ---
# Path to an installed episodic-memory plugin. Unset = degrade gracefully.
# SILL_EPISODIC_MEMORY_PATH=
